WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
A lower rate doesn't tell you everything

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.460
about a loan offer.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.260
Look at what you're comparing before choosing.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.440
Are the estimates for the same purchase,

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.940
down payment and loan term?

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.260
Were they prepared on different dates?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.400
Then look at the monthly payment, the

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.520
costs it includes and the cash needed

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.240
at closing. Points or lender credits belong

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.580
in that comparison, too.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:23.360
Ask the lender to explain differences and

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.400
missing amounts. The comparison worksheet keeps two

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.660
estimates and your questions together.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.960
Review your answers before sending them to

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.530
me, or print the comparison for yourself.
